Pinned items can now be reordered via drag & drop. Order persists to localStorage.

## Changes

- **DragDropManager**: Centralized drag & drop handler with state tracking, visual feedback, and reorder logic
  - Drag handle (`⋮⋮`) indicator on pinned items
  - Semi-transparent drag state (opacity: 0.4)
  - Blue drop indicator line showing target position
  - Position calculation based on mouse Y relative to item midpoint

- **Integration**: Applied to both title-only and full view rendering modes
  - Only pinned items are draggable
  - Pinned items maintain position above unpinned items after reorder
  - Immediate save on drop

## Implementation

```javascript
const DragDropManager = {
  setupDraggable(listItem, pinnedIndex, allData, onReorder) {
    listItem.setAttribute('draggable', 'true');
    // Add drag handle, event listeners for dragstart/dragover/drop
  },

  reorderPinnedItems(fromIndex, toIndex, allData, onReorder) {
    const pinnedItems = allData.filter(item => item.pinned);
    const [movedItem] = pinnedItems.splice(fromIndex, 1);
    pinnedItems.splice(toIndex, 0, movedItem);
    // Reconstruct data array and trigger save
  }
}
```

Drag events handle opacity transitions, drop indicator positioning (before/after target based on midpoint), and index adjustment for upward vs downward movement.

